{
  "method": "For each publication-time bin, sum termination.count across all epochs only where prior_epoch_outcome=false. This counts each root with an observed outcome once, including roots whose first observed outcome is finalized. Exclude forked=true for non-fork rates. Receipt rates sum finalization.count across all epochs and carried/fresh groups, as in the main comparison.",
  "limitations": [
    "This is reconstructed publication timing for observed roots, not an independent publisher counter. Missing-outcome roots would be absent.",
    "For these seven captures, deduplicated observed roots across both fork classes equal published_blocks=50000, so no aggregate publication coverage gap is visible.",
    "The publication timestamp is taken immediately before serialization/TCP writes, not at peer receipt. Shared-host generation, transport, and observation scheduling are not isolated.",
    "Receipt windows can include backlog from preceding publication windows; early and late differences are descriptive, not a causal decomposition.",
    "The 25-second publication bin is a partial tail; phase comparisons use 5-10 and 15-25 seconds only."
